armGBA-pico patch to upstream armGBA (src/cpu/jit.c), MPL-2.0 like the file it changes.
Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by build.sh to a copy in out/src.

Upstream sizes the code memory at an eighth of the RAM the system reports. The LK has no such
figure: the host says how much a machine's code memory gets (armgbaHostCodeSize), the size the
build sets (ARMGBA_HOST_CODE_MIB), or less for the netplay pair's second machine, which shares the
heap with the first. A smaller code memory only reclaims its slots sooner.

--- a/src/cpu/jit.c
+++ b/src/cpu/jit.c
@@ -2955,7 +2955,14 @@
 	        (unsigned long long) jit->stepped, (unsigned long long) jit->carefulSteps, (unsigned long long) jit->exits[EXIT_EXACT]);
 }
 
-#if !defined(__3DS__)
+#if defined(ARMGBA_HOST_CODE_MIB)
+// The host says how much code memory a machine gets: it has no RAM figure to take an eighth of, and
+// for netplay a second machine shares the heap with the first, so it may get less than the most.
+extern size_t armgbaHostCodeSize(size_t most);
+static size_t codeSizeFor(void) {
+	return armgbaHostCodeSize((size_t) ARMGBA_HOST_CODE_MIB << 20);
+}
+#elif !defined(__3DS__)
 // An eighth of the RAM the system reports, in whole MiB, from CODE_SIZE_MIN to CODE_SIZE: 16 MiB on
 // a Miyoo Mini (128 MB, less what Linux keeps), where a game filling more could leave too little
 // for the rest, and 32 MiB from 256 MB up. Nothing is in memory until a game fills it.
